  "actions": [
    {
      "category": "offensive",
      "cost": "free",
      "description": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If the Gardener's next action is to cast a 6th- or lower level spell, reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action).</p>",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "day"
      },
      "name": "Quickened Casting",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "spellshape"
      ],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "offensive",
      "cost": "2",
      "description": "<p>The ghost stares at a creature it can see within 30 feet. The target takes @Damage[9d6[void]] damage with a @Check[will|dc:37|basic] save.</p>\n<p>A creature that fails its save is also Stupefied 1 for 1 minute.</p>",
      "frequency": null,
      "name": "Corrupting Gaze",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "offensive",
      "cost": "2",
      "description": "<p>With a touch, the ghost attempts to drain a living creature's life force. It makes a ghostly hand Strike but deals no damage on a hit.</p>\n<p>Instead, the target becomes Drained 1 for 1 day, and the ghost regains @Damage[(max(1,floor(@actor.level/2)))[healing]]{HP equal to half its own level}.</p>",
      "frequency": null,
      "name": "Draining Touch",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "offensive",
      "cost": "2",
      "description": "<p>The ghost cries out in pain and anguish as small objects and debris fly about in a @Template[emanation|distance:30]. Creatures in this area take @Damage[9d6[bludgeoning]] damage, subject to a @Check[reflex|dc:37|basic] save.</p>",
      "frequency": null,
      "name": "Telekinetic Assault",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [
        "divine"
      ],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "defensive",
      "cost": "passive",
      "description": "<p>Releasing the nereid and allowing her to leave this place (or, alternatively, killing her) allows the Gardener to move on to the afterlife.</p>\n<p>When a ghost is destroyed, it re-forms after [[/br 2d4 #days]]{2d4 days} within the location it's bound to, fully healed. A ghost can be permanently destroyed only if someone determines the reason for its existence and sets right whatever prevents the spirit from resting.</p>",
      "frequency": null,
      "name": "Rejuvenation",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [
        "divine"
      ],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "interaction",
      "cost": "passive",
      "description": "<p>A typical ghost can stray only a short distance from where it was killed or the place it haunts. A typical limit is 120 feet. Some ghosts are instead bound to a room, building, item, or creature that was special to it rather than a location.</p>",
      "frequency": null,
      "name": "Site Bound",
      "requirements": null,
      "traits": [],
      "trigger": null
    },
    {
      "category": "defensive",
      "cost": "passive",
